logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"doi":"10.1016/j.ejmech.2025.118221","year":2026,"record_id":"MLDB-004704","detection":"HPLC","method_description":"The Log P value of complex 10k was determined using the shake flask method. A mixture of 50 mL n-octanol and 50 mL water (PBS, pH = 7.4) was prepared and shaken at room temperature for 24 h. The mixture was then centrifuged to thoroughly separate the two phases, yielding a water-saturated n-octanol solution and an n-octanol-saturated water solution. A certain weight of complex 10k was dissolved in n-octanol pre-saturated with water (PBS), and then the complex solution was mixed with different volumes of PBS (pre-saturated with n-octanol). After shaking for 24 h, the complex concentration of each phase was determined by HPLC, and the Log P value was calculated. Log P = Log (Co/Cw), where Co is the concentration of complex 10k in n-octanol, and Cw is the concentration of complex 10k in the water phase. All experiments were done in triplicate."}]}